const command = req.body.command;
const buffer = Buffer.alloc(1024);
buffer.fill(0);
buffer[0] = 0x00; // this is the vulnerability
exec(command);
```

This code first receives the command in `req.body.command`. It then allocates 1024 bytes of memory and fills the first byte with 0x00. This is a common buffer overflow vulnerability. If the command length is longer than 1024 bytes, the extra bytes will be written to the next memory location, potentially overwriting the next instructions in memory. This allows the attacker to execute arbitrary code.

